#: includes/help/account-articles.php:16
#: includes/help/account-articles.php:33
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:22
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:48
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:68
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:17
msgid "How listing works"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:18
msgid "From your first draft to a live listing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:20
msgid ""
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Open <a href=\"{url:submit}\">Add property</a> and go through the five steps: Basics, Details, Photos, Location, Review.</li>\n"
"<li>Click <strong>Save draft</strong> at any time – nothing is public until you submit.</li>\n"
"<li>On the last step click <strong>Submit for review</strong>. Our team checks the listing, usually within one working day.</li>\n"
"<li>You get an email when it is live, or when something needs changing.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p>Your listings, with their status and views, are on <a href=\"{url:listings}\">My listings</a>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:34
msgid "What each status means"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:35
msgid "Draft, Pending review, Needs changes, Live, Sold and Let."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:37
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Draft</strong> – only you can see it. Finish it and submit when ready.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Pending review</strong> – waiting for our team. You can still open it, but changes wait for the review.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Needs changes</strong> – our team sent it back. The reason is shown on the listing and in your email. Click <strong>Fix and resubmit</strong>.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Live</strong> – visible to everyone and in search. The eye icon shows how many times it has been viewed.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Sold / Let</strong> – still online with a ribbon, but no longer in search. Click <strong>Relist</strong> if it becomes available again. Short stays you mark unavailable show as Let.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:50
#: includes/help/account-articles.php:67
#: includes/help/account-articles.php:84
msgid "Your listing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:51
msgid "Taking good photos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:52
msgid "Listings with clear photos get far more enquiries."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:54
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li>Hold your phone <strong>sideways</strong> (landscape) and keep it level.</li>\n"
"<li>Shoot in daylight with curtains open and lights on. Tidy each room first.</li>\n"
"<li>Include every room and at least one photo of the outside, the view and the parking.</li>\n"
"<li>Add at least 3 photos; 10–20 is better. JPG, PNG or WebP up to 8 MB each – large photos are made smaller before upload.</li>\n"
"<li>The first photo is the cover. Use <strong>Make cover photo</strong> to change it, and drag to reorder.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:68
msgid "Getting approved first time"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:69
msgid "What our team checks before a listing goes live."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:71
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Title</strong> says what and where, e.g. “3 Bedroom Apartment, Kilimani”.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Price</strong> is the real asking price, and for rentals the period (per month, per year…). Short stays are priced per night.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Description</strong> covers size, rooms, condition, what is included and what is nearby.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Location</strong> uses a nearby road or landmark, not the house number. The pin stays private: visitors only see a shaded area.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Photos</strong> are your own, clear and show the actual property.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:85
msgid "Edit, mark sold or let, and delete"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:86
msgid "Keep your listings up to date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:88
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Edit</strong> – change anything and save. On some sites edits to a live listing are checked again before they show.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Mark sold / Mark let</strong> – use this as soon as the deal is done so people stop calling about it.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Relist</strong> – makes a sold or let listing available again.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Delete</strong> – tap twice to confirm. This cannot be undone; marking as sold or let is usually better.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:100
#: includes/help/account-articles.php:116
#: includes/help/account-articles.php:131
msgid "Enquiries & account"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:101
msgid "Answering enquiries"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:102
msgid "Where messages from buyers and tenants appear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:104
msgid ""
"<p>Messages about your listings are emailed to you and listed on <a href=\"{url:enquiries-tab}\">Enquiries</a>, with the person’s name, phone and email.</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>Reply quickly – the first person to answer usually gets the deal.</li>\n"
"<li>Use the call, WhatsApp or email buttons next to each enquiry.</li>\n"
"<li>Never send a deposit or ID details to someone you have not met. Report anything suspicious to us.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:117
msgid "Your profile and password"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:118
msgid "Change your name, phone, email or password."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:120
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li>Update your details on <a href=\"{url:profile}\">Profile</a>. Agents can also change the photo and bio on their public agent page.</li>\n"
"<li>To change your password, type a new one in <em>New password</em> on Profile and click <em>Save profile</em>.</li>\n"
"<li>Forgot your password? Use <em>Forgot your password?</em> on the sign-in form.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:132
msgid "Questions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:133
msgid "Quick answers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/account-articles.php:135
msgid ""
"<p><strong>How long does review take?</strong> Usually within one working day.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Why was my listing sent back?</strong> The reason is on the listing under <em>Needs changes</em> and in your email. Fix it and click <em>Submit for review</em> again.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>I cannot see “Add property”.</strong> Your account may still be waiting for approval, or listing may be paused on this site. Contact us.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Can someone else manage my listing?</strong> Ask us to assign one of our agents.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:23
msgid "Welcome to Makaazi"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:24
msgid "What the theme and the two plugins do, and where everything lives."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:27
msgid ""
"<p>Makaazi is a property listing template by <a href=\"https://ascensiondynamics.co/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ascension Dynamics</a>. It is made of three parts that work together:</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Makaazi theme</strong> – the look of the site: header, footer, page layouts, fonts and colours.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Makaazi Core plugin</strong> – properties, search and filters, property pages, maps, enquiries, agents, owner accounts, favourites and compare.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Makaazi Hero Slider plugin</strong> – the big image slider with the Buy/Rent search bar on the home page.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Everything you manage is under the <strong>Properties</strong> menu on the left:</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:properties}\">All Properties</a> and <a href=\"{url:new}\">Add New</a> – your listings.</li>\n"
"<li>Statuses (Buy / Rent), Uses, Types, Categories, Locations, Features – the lists used in search and filters.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:slider}\">Hero Sliders</a>, <a href=\"{url:agents}\">Agents</a>, <a href=\"{url:enquiries}\">Enquiries</a>.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings}\">Settings</a>, <a href=\"{url:shortcodes}\">Shortcodes</a>, <a href=\"{url:demo}\">Demo Content</a> and this Help Center.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>New site? Start with {help:demo}, then {help:add-property}.</p>\n"
"<p class=\"mk-help__tip\">Look for the <strong>Help</strong> button at the top right of any Makaazi screen. It shows tips for that screen.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:49
msgid "Import the demo content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:50
msgid "Fill an empty site with sample listings, agents, a slider and ready-made pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:53
msgid ""
"<p>The demo gives you a working site in one click, so you can see how everything fits before adding your own listings.</p>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Go to <a href=\"{url:demo}\">Properties › Demo Content</a>.</li>\n"
"<li>Click <strong>Import demo content</strong>. It takes about a minute because it copies the photos.</li>\n"
"<li>Visit the site. The home page, Properties page, agent pages, Favourites, Compare and My account are all set up.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p>What gets added: 15 properties in Nairobi, Mombasa and Nakuru, 4 agents, the home page slider, the pages above, the main menu and sensible settings.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Removing it:</strong> the same screen has a <strong>Remove demo content</strong> button. It deletes only what the import created; anything you added yourself stays. You can import again at any time.</p>\n"
"<p class=\"mk-help__tip\">Tip: replace demo listings with real ones one by one, then remove the demo when you are done.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:69
msgid "Launch checklist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:70
msgid "The settings to check before you share the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:73
msgid ""
"<ol>\n"
"<li><strong>Logo and site name</strong> – Appearance › Editor › Patterns › Header, or Settings › General for the site title.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Contact details</strong> – <a href=\"{url:settings:single}\">Settings › Property page</a>: contact name, phone, WhatsApp number (format 2547…, no +) and the email that receives enquiries.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Currency and units</strong> – <a href=\"{url:settings:general}\">Settings › General</a>.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Price brackets</strong> – <a href=\"{url:settings:prices}\">Settings › Price brackets</a>, so the price filters match your market.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Features</strong> – <a href=\"{url:settings:features}\">Settings › Features</a>: switch agents and owner submissions on or off.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Permalinks</strong> – Settings › Permalinks should be “Post name”. Click <em>Save</em> there once if a property page shows “Not found”.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Email</strong> – send yourself a test enquiry from a property page. If it does not arrive, see {help:email}.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Remove demo content</strong> if you imported it.</li>\n"
"</ol>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:92
msgid "Add or edit a property"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:93
msgid "Every field on the property screen, in the order you fill it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:96
msgid ""
"<ol>\n"
"<li><strong>Title</strong> – e.g. “4 Bedroom Townhouse, Lavington”. It becomes the page address.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Description</strong> – the main text box. Short paragraphs read best on phones.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Right-hand column</strong> – choose the <em>Status</em> (For Sale, For Rent or Short Stay), <em>Use</em> (residential or commercial), <em>Type</em>, <em>Category</em>, <em>Location</em> and tick the <em>Features</em>. Pick the most specific location (e.g. Kilimani, not Nairobi); the parents are added automatically.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Property Details box</strong>, tab by tab:\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li><em>Listing</em> – Featured (shows first and gets a badge), availability (Available, Under offer, Sold, Let) and the reference number (created on save).</li>\n"
"<li><em>Pricing</em> – the amount and, for rentals, per month / year / night. Tick “Price on request” to hide the number.</li>\n"
"<li><em>Specs</em> – bedrooms, bathrooms, parking, floor area, land size, year built.</li>\n"
"<li><em>Gallery</em> – add photos, drag to reorder. The first photo is the cover on cards.</li>\n"
"<li><em>Location</em> – drag the pin to the exact spot, then choose the public privacy radius (see {help:map-privacy}).</li>\n"
"<li><em>Attributes</em> – extra rows for the Details table, e.g. “Service charge – KES 8,000 /month”, plus a video or virtual tour link.</li>\n"
"</ul></li>\n"
"<li><strong>Agent</strong> box – who handles this listing (or “Site contact”). Enquiries go to that agent.</li>\n"
"<li>Click <strong>Publish</strong>.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p class=\"mk-help__tip\">Sold and Let listings stay online with a ribbon but drop out of search and grids. Use this instead of deleting, so links keep working.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:120
msgid "Photo guide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:121
msgid "Sizes and order that make listings look their best."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:124
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li>Landscape photos, at least <strong>1600 px wide</strong>. Phone photos are fine; hold the phone sideways.</li>\n"
"<li>Put the best outside or living-room shot first – it is the cover on cards and in search.</li>\n"
"<li>6–20 photos per listing. Cards let visitors swipe through the first few (Settings › Cards › Photos per card).</li>\n"
"<li>WordPress makes smaller copies automatically, so you do not need to resize.</li>\n"
"<li>Photos open in a full-screen lightbox with arrows and swipe on the property page.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:138
msgid "Maps and location privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:139
msgid "Why the map shows a circle, and how to change it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:142
msgid ""
"<p>Property pages show the general area as a shaded circle, not the exact house. The exact pin you place is kept private – it is never sent to visitors’ browsers.</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>Set the circle size per listing in <em>Property Details › Location › Public privacy radius</em>, or the default in <a href=\"{url:settings:single}\">Settings › Property page</a>.</li>\n"
"<li>Tick <em>Show the exact pin publicly</em> only for places that are already public, such as an office block, shop or development.</li>\n"
"<li>Maps use OpenStreetMap, which is free. For a busy site, use a paid tile provider and paste its URL in Settings › Property page › Map tiles URL.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:155
msgid "Short Stays (nightly rentals)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:156
msgid "List furnished homes that guests book by the night."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:159
msgid ""
"<p>Short Stay is a third listing type next to Buy and Rent, for holiday homes and serviced apartments priced per night.</p>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Make sure <em>Short Stays</em> is ticked in <a href=\"{url:settings:features}\">Settings › Features</a>.</li>\n"
"<li>Add a property and choose the <em>Short Stay</em> status. The price period switches to <em>Per night</em>.</li>\n"
"<li>Use <em>Attributes</em> for stay details: Sleeps, Minimum stay, Check-in time, Cleaning.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p>Visitors get a <strong>Short Stay</strong> tab in the search bar and filters, with nightly price ranges you set in <a href=\"{url:settings:prices}\">Settings › Price brackets</a>. Put a row of stays on any page with <code>[makaazi_properties source=\"stay\" layout=\"carousel\"]</code>.</p>\n"
"<p>When a stay is no longer offered, owners click <em>Mark unavailable</em> (you can set Availability to Let). Makaazi shows availability and takes enquiries; it does not take bookings or payments.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:175
msgid "Manage the lists visitors filter by."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:178
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Locations</strong> are nested: City › Area (e.g. Nairobi › Westlands). Give each area a photo – it is used by the Locations tiles on the home page.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Types</strong> are what the building is (Apartment, Villa, Office…). <strong>Categories</strong> group listings for marketing (Luxury, New development…).</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Uses</strong> are Residential or Commercial. <strong>Statuses</strong> are For Sale, For Rent and Short Stay – the Buy / Rent / Short Stay choice in search.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Features</strong> are the ticks on the property page (Borehole, Backup generator, Pool…).</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Renaming a term updates every listing that uses it. Deleting a term removes it from listings but does not delete the listings.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:193
msgid "Where messages from visitors go and how to follow them up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:196
msgid ""
"<p>Every message sent from a property page or the contact page is saved under <a href=\"{url:enquiries}\">Properties › Enquiries</a> and emailed.</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>If the listing has an agent, the email goes to the agent. Tick <em>Copy me on agent enquiries</em> in Settings › Features to get a copy.</li>\n"
"<li>Otherwise it goes to <em>Send enquiries to</em> in Settings › Property page (or the site admin email).</li>\n"
"<li>Owners get an email for enquiries on their own listings and can read them in their dashboard.</li>\n"
"<li>Each enquiry shows the property, name, phone and email. Reply by phone, WhatsApp or email.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Spam protection is built in: a hidden trap field and a limit of a few messages per visitor per hour.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:212
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:233
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:252
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:277
msgid "Home page & design"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:213
msgid "Hero slider"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:214
msgid "Slides, timing, the search bar, and placing a slider on a page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:217
msgid ""
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Go to <a href=\"{url:slider}\">Properties › Hero Sliders</a> and open a slider (or add a new one).</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Slides</strong> – add a background image (1920 × 1080 or larger), an optional phone image, label, heading, text and up to two buttons. Drag to reorder. <em>Show from / until</em> dates let you schedule a promotion.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Slides from</strong> – your slides, your featured properties, or both.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Slider settings</strong> – effect (fade, slide, slow zoom), autoplay timing, arrows/dots/progress bar and the height on desktop, tablet and phone.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Search bar</strong> – show the Buy/Rent search, choose its position and style, tick the fields and drag to reorder them.</li>\n"
"<li>Click <strong>Update</strong>, then copy the shortcode from the box on the right.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p>To show a slider: paste the shortcode, e.g. <code>[makaazi_slider slug=\"home\"]</code>, into a Shortcode block, or use the Hero Slider widget in Elementor.</p>\n"
"<p class=\"mk-help__tip\">Visitors who have “reduce motion” turned on never get autoplay or zoom.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:234
msgid "Edit the home page and other pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:235
msgid "Change sections, headings and the header and footer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:238
msgid ""
"<p>Pages are built from blocks. Most Makaazi sections are a <strong>Shortcode block</strong> with one line in it, such as <code>[makaazi_properties featured=\"1\" columns=\"3\"]</code>.</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Home page</strong> – Pages › Home. Click a section to edit its heading, or change the numbers in a shortcode to show more or fewer listings. See {help:shortcodes} for every option.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Header and footer</strong> – Appearance › Editor › Patterns, then Header or Footer. Logo, menu and contact details are there.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Colours and fonts</strong> – Appearance › Editor › Styles.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Menu</strong> – in the Header, click the Navigation block.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Prefer drag and drop? Install Elementor and use the Makaazi widgets – see {help:elementor}.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:253
msgid "Using shortcodes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:254
msgid "Put listings, search, maps and forms on any page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:257
msgid ""
"<p>A shortcode is a short tag in square brackets that shows a Makaazi section. The full list, with every option and copy buttons, is on <a href=\"{url:shortcodes}\">Properties › Shortcodes</a>.</p>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>Edit a page and add a <strong>Shortcode</strong> block (type <code>/shortcode</code>).</li>\n"
"<li>Paste the shortcode and change the options, e.g. <code>[makaazi_properties status=\"rent\" location=\"westlands\" columns=\"4\" limit=\"8\"]</code>.</li>\n"
"<li>Update the page.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p>Most used:</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li><code>[makaazi_properties]</code> – a grid, list or carousel of listings (featured, buy, rent, by location…).</li>\n"
"<li><code>[makaazi_listing]</code> – the full Properties page with filters, sort and map view.</li>\n"
"<li><code>[makaazi_search]</code> – a search bar that sends visitors to the Properties page.</li>\n"
"<li><code>[makaazi_locations]</code>, <code>[makaazi_agents]</code>, <code>[makaazi_favourites]</code>, <code>[makaazi_compare]</code>, <code>[makaazi_dashboard]</code>.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p class=\"mk-help__tip\">Options use plain words – use the slug shown on the Locations or Types screen, e.g. <code>location=\"kilimani\"</code>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:278
msgid "Elementor widgets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:279
msgid "Drag-and-drop Makaazi sections when Elementor is installed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:282
msgid ""
"<p>When the free Elementor plugin is active, a <strong>Makaazi</strong> group appears in the Elementor widget panel:</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li>Hero Slider, Property Search, Properties (grid, list or carousel), Property Listing (full page with filters), Locations, Agents.</li>\n"
"<li>Property Section – one part of a property page (gallery, facts, details, features, map, contact, similar listings) for building your own property template in Elementor Pro.</li>\n"
"<li>Favourites &amp; Compare.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Each widget has the same options as its shortcode on the <em>Content</em> tab, and colours, fonts and spacing on the <em>Style</em> tab. Widgets show live previews in the editor.</p>\n"
"<p>Elementor is optional. The theme works fully without it.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:298
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:319
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:344
msgid "Agents & owners"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:300
msgid "Agent profiles, agent sign-in, and assigning listings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:303
msgid ""
"<p>Agents are switched on in <a href=\"{url:settings:features}\">Settings › Features</a>. Turning them off hides agent pages and the agent box on listings; nothing is deleted.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Add an agent</strong></p>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:agents}\">Properties › Agents</a> › Add New.</li>\n"
"<li>Name (the title), bio (the text box), <em>Agent photo</em> (square, at least 400 px) and, in <em>Agent details</em>, job title, office, phone, WhatsApp and email.</li>\n"
"<li>Optional: in <em>Sign-in account</em>, pick a user (or click <em>Create a user</em>) so the agent can sign in. The user is given the Agent role.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p><strong>What signed-in agents can do:</strong> add and edit their own listings from the website dashboard or wp-admin, read enquiries for their listings, and update their profile. They cannot see other agents’ listings or change settings.</p>\n"
"<p>With <em>Review agent listings</em> on, an agent’s new listings wait in <a href=\"{url:pending}\">Pending</a> for you to approve.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Assign a listing:</strong> edit the property and choose the agent in the Agent box. Their card appears on the property page and enquiries go to them.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:320
msgid "Owner sign-ups and listing review"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:321
msgid "Let property owners list from the website, and approve or reject their listings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:324
msgid ""
"<p>Switch on <em>Owner submissions</em> in <a href=\"{url:settings:features}\">Settings › Features</a> and choose how owners get an account:</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Anyone can sign up</strong> – optionally with <em>Confirm email</em>.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Sign-ups need my approval</strong> – new owners appear under <a href=\"{url:users}\">Users</a> as “Pending”. Hover and click <strong>Activate</strong>.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Invite only</strong> – you create users with the role <em>Property owner</em>.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Owners use the <strong>My account</strong> page (it contains <code>[makaazi_dashboard]</code>). They never see wp-admin.</p>\n"
"<p><strong>Reviewing a listing</strong></p>\n"
"<ol>\n"
"<li>A number on the Properties menu shows listings waiting. Open <a href=\"{url:pending}\">Pending</a>.</li>\n"
"<li>Open the listing to check photos, price and text. You can fix small things yourself.</li>\n"
"<li>Back in the list, hover the row: <strong>Approve</strong> publishes it and emails the owner. <strong>Reject</strong> asks for a reason, moves it back to draft and emails the owner the reason.</li>\n"
"</ol>\n"
"<p>With <em>Review edits to live listings</em> on, an owner’s changes to a live listing go back to Pending.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:345
msgid "Favourites and compare"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:346
msgid "How visitors save and compare listings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:349
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li>Visitors tap the <strong>heart</strong> on a card or <strong>Save</strong> on a property page. Saved listings are kept in the browser, and in their account when signed in, so they follow them to other devices.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Compare</strong> holds up to 4 listings and shows them side by side, with differences highlighted.</li>\n"
"<li>Both pages have a <em>Share</em> link that opens the same list for someone else.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p>Switch each on or off and choose the pages in <a href=\"{url:settings:shortlist}\">Settings › Favourites &amp; compare</a>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:364
msgid "Settings explained"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:365
msgid "What each Settings tab controls."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:368
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings:features}\"><strong>Features</strong></a> – switch Short Stays, agents and owner submissions on or off, and how they work. Switching off hides things; nothing is deleted.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings:general}\"><strong>General</strong></a> – currency, short prices (KES 85M), m² or ft², the unit switch and the reference prefix.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings:cards}\"><strong>Cards</strong></a> – button text, how many photos a card can scroll, photo shape, what each card shows and the “New” badge.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings:listing}\"><strong>Properties page</strong></a> – listings per page, default sort and which filters to offer.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings:shortlist}\"><strong>Favourites &amp; compare</strong></a> – switches and pages.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings:single}\"><strong>Property page</strong></a> – contact details, where enquiries go, map privacy, similar listings and map tiles.</li>\n"
"<li><a href=\"{url:settings:prices}\"><strong>Price brackets</strong></a> – amounts offered in the price filters for Buy, Rent (per month) and Short Stay (per night).</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:385
msgid "Google, sharing and Yoast SEO"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:386
msgid "How listings appear in Google and when shared on WhatsApp or Facebook."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:389
msgid ""
"<p>Makaazi tells search engines what each listing is (price, rooms, size, area, photos) using Schema.org data, so Google can show richer results. Nothing to set up.</p>\n"
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Without an SEO plugin</strong>, Makaazi adds a description, the share preview (title, price, area and cover photo for WhatsApp, Facebook and X) and sensible titles such as “Properties to rent”.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>With Yoast SEO or Rank Math</strong>, the plugin takes over titles and share tags and Makaazi feeds it: the listing data joins its schema, listings without a written meta description get an automatic one, gallery photos go into the XML sitemap, and Yoast’s content analysis also reads the Property Details box.</li>\n"
"<li>In Yoast you can use these variables in title and description templates (Yoast SEO › Settings › Content types › Properties): <code>%%mk_price%%</code>, <code>%%mk_location%%</code>, <code>%%mk_status%%</code>, <code>%%mk_type%%</code>, <code>%%mk_beds%%</code>, <code>%%mk_ref%%</code>. Example title: <code>%%title%% – %%mk_price%% %%sep%% %%sitename%%</code>.</li>\n"
"<li>Search pages with several filters are marked “noindex” so Google indexes your clean pages (Properties, Properties to rent, each location) instead of thousands of combinations.</li>\n"
"<li>Exact map pins are never shared with Google either.</li>\n"
"</ul>\n"
"<p class=\"mk-help__tip\">Tip: write a short, specific first sentence in each description. It is what Google and WhatsApp show.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:406
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:422
#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:440
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:407
msgid "Emails are not arriving"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:408
msgid "Enquiry, approval and sign-up emails need a working mail setup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:411
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>On your own computer (XAMPP, Local…)</strong> email is not sent by default. Enquiries are still saved under Properties › Enquiries, and you can activate owners under Users.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>On a live host</strong>, install an SMTP plugin (e.g. WP Mail SMTP) and connect it to your email provider. This also stops emails landing in spam.</li>\n"
"<li>Check the address in Settings › Property page › Send enquiries to.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:423
msgid "A page says “Not found” or a shortcode shows as text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:424
msgid "Fixes for the most common display problems."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help/admin-articles.php:427
msgid ""
"<ul>\n"
"<li><strong>Property or agent page “Not found”</strong> – go to Settings › Permalinks and click <em>Save Changes</em> (no need to change anything).</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Shortcode shows as plain text</strong> – check Makaazi Core is active and the shortcode is spelled correctly. Put it in a Shortcode block, not a Paragraph.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Agent pages missing</strong> – agents are switched off in Settings › Features.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Listing missing from search</strong> – it is Sold/Let, a draft, or waiting in Pending.</li>\n"
"<li><strong>Map is grey</strong> – the listing has no pin. Edit it and drag the pin in Property Details › Location.</li>\n"
"</ul>"
msgstr ""

